==Strategy==
The key to beating this stage is to '''always''' have at least one expensive backliner unit ready to deploy. If you were to send them all out around the same time and one of them goes down, you can safely assume that the rest will soon follow suit, leaving you defenseless and thus causing you to lose ground (unless if you have a good stack of [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cats]])—having a heavy attacker off cooldown whenever possible somewhat alleviates this problem. You should bring 4 meatshields at minimum, 5 ideally to prevent the Capies from easily killing your backliners and to fill in gaps better when Manic Eraser attacks.

Like in the original stage, [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] and [[Battle Items#Cat CPU|Cat CPU]] are highly recommended for most approaches. Sniper provides much-needed knockback to Manic Eraser and CPU if you don't feel like pressing boxes for 20 minutes. The use of at least 4 meatshields is advised, and mandatory if the player's cat levels are not high enough. Be prepared with other bulky attackers, as a Gory Dark triad will spawn a little after starting the level. Having [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] makes the start a lot easier, as she can keep the Gories on a constant cycle of knockback '''IF''' she is level 30, otherwise, she'll be a bit short on damage. Be aware of the strong peons supporting Manic Eraser Cat, and try to hold off on triggering the base until after killing the Owlbrow trio, this will give the player enough money to have a better chance at taking on Manic Eraser and co. Manic Eraser is the only enemy that spawns upon hitting the base, so optimally you should stall to kill the first starting Capies.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] - Very powerful midranger against the Gory Darks, a bulky attacker and is quite cost efficient for what you get.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] - An extremely long ranged Crowd-Controller, his main role is to slow the peons and Manic Eraser, preventing all of them from pushing too far.
*[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Recruit]] - Similar to Cyberpunk, but much better suited against Manic Eraser and less against the peons. The true form grants more range for better safety and the ability to Slow which stalls Manic Eraser even further.
*[[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]]/[[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Lizard Cat]] - Because of Manic Eraser's high range, these two are good choices since they stack up and deal gradual damage to Manic Eraser over time, along with being able to deal with peons nicely.
*[[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] - Even though it's inconsistent, Ururun Wolf's knockback ability along with her high range (higher than Manic Eraser!) is able to push Manic Eraser back to its base to regain any lost ground, however if she was to proc knockback against the base too much, it may cause your other backliners to slowly move into Manic Eraser's range, so use her with caution. She MUST be level 30 to knockback Gory Dark in one hit which is very important since you have to keep your ground against them.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] - Crazed Bahamut should always be used over Awakened Bahamut in this stage, seeing as backliners are better for this stage rather than a suicidal rusher unit. Although Bahamut has a high damage per hit, his TBA is simply too high to be used as a reliable damage source against Manic Eraser, so he's better used as a way to nuke the peons. Only use Bahamut Cat if you have no better Uber Super Rares.
*[[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross Cat/Manic Macho Legs]] - If one has no better options for a piercing unit to chip the Owlbrows, Crazed Gross can help out a lot as long as there is a stepping stone that allows for him to release his waves. His True Form provides a longer reach.
*[[Brainwashed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Gross Cat]] - Crazed Gross but with higher potential damage thanks to the Surge hitting multiple times, though a stepping stone is needed lest he dies to Manic Eraser.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - An extremely disposable unit that is able to deliver serious damage against the Capies. He has a low cost of 690, and delivers enough damage to at least knock back the Gory Darks once and can chip the Owlbrows, though against Gory Dark he may struggle due to his blindspot. He isn't guaranteed to always get hits on Manic Eraser or the Capies, as the Capies sit quite far from your frontline and Manic Eraser's fast attack rate can clear Courier before he even reaches.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Uber backliners with 430+ range - While Manic Eraser has 390 range, it is much better to use Uber Rares with 430+ range since only outranging by 5 or 10 is enough for Manic Eraser to kill them if the frontline shifts even just a little bit.
*[[Long Distance]]/[[Omni Strike]] Ubers - Ubers with piercing range help a lot on this stage, as they can hit the Owlbrows from behind Manic Eraser, and can potentially even destroy the base before Manic Eraser dies if fighting close enough. Some good examples are [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Aphrodite]], [[Sea Serpent Daliasan (Uber Rare Cat)|Daliasan]], and [[Lucifer the Fallen (Uber Rare Cat)|Lucifer]].
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Tesalan/Lufalan Pasalan]] - It can outrange all enemies here, and its very high damage combined with critical hits can speed up the endurance battle dramatically. However, be wary of peons due to its single-target attacks. The True Form has improved range, making it helpful to have in case the enemies push, as well as greater overall damage from the higher critical chance.
*[[Shadow Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Diabolic Gao]] - Has decent DPS for general use, good range but most importantly a 1-second freeze and massive damage to Traitless enemies.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Super Galaxy Cosmo]] - Has extreme range and can knockback the Owlbrows, able to catch essentially everything on the stage. Has a very slow attack rate, but given the nature of the stage's threats, it's usually negligible. You'll just have to make sure not to use the Cat Cannon when he's not attacking as he might suicidally rush into Manic Eraser's range.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Jizo's Moving Castle]] - While his First Form is great, what you'll want here more is his second form, who not only acts as a better Bahamut Cat, but also nukes the Gory Darks out of existence instantly compared to Pizza Cat.
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny, Phonoa]]/[[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]] - Both have over 500 range, King of Destiny Phonoa does massive damage to anything that has a trait and can hit up to 1,000 range while King of Extinction Phono slow anything for 2 seconds and can hit up to 900 range, usually hitting the base. This amount of piercing allows it to easily destroy the enemy base long before Manic Eraser itself.
*[[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai Pai DX]] - A really strong Uber for this stage, she can chip Manic Eraser without issue, and she can massively help with the Capies since she deals massive damage to them. She also can tank a Manic Eraser hit and survive. With proper meatshielding, she can be a great ranged attacker.
*[[Emperor Cat (Legend Rare Cat)|Tyrant Cat]] - A decent damage dealer who outranges Manic Eraser by a whopping 161 range, so he can stay safe most of the time and can get hit once by the boss and survive. Also inflicts negative effects on the peons, but that should be treated as a bonus.
*[[Akechi Mitsuhide (Uber Rare Cat)|Wargod Mitsuhide]] - Mitsuhide outranges every enemy in this stage, deals decent damage, and even has the Conjure ability, which in this case summons a spirit that knocks back everything in its range. He also has a 50% activation chance for a level 3 Surge Attack. Bringing Mitsuhide is a great option for many reasons, including the decent price of 4500, and the many knockbacks.
*[[Seaside Pegasa (Uber Rare Cat)|Seaside Pegasa v]] - Completely outranging Manic Eraser Cat and capable of reliably Weakening two of the three primary pushers of this stage (including the boss) with up to an 80% uptime and 733 effective range through Mini-Wave, Seaside Pegasa is everything you could ask for in a crowd-controller and more. She even has a very powerful Conjure!
*[[Spooky Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Spooky Thundia]] - Can not only outrange Manic Eraser but can also oneshot the Gory Darks, which is helpful to prevent them from pushing. Additionally serves as a general nuker like Crazed Bahamut Cat.
*[[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Squire Luno]] - It is recommended to use his first form, due to cost and just needing his spirit. Although he can not outrange Manic Eraser, you can send him out and time his Conjure. This can effectively keep Manic Eraser and the rest of the peons stuck at the base, whilst chipping down Manic Eraser.
*[[Lone Moon Lunos (Uber Rare Cat)|Lunos the Eclipsed]] - Able to knock back Manic Eraser, Lunos the Eclipsed completely destroys this stage by trivializing one of the biggest threats here. Not to mention the fact that his Conjured spirit can easily burst down the supporting troops, and for Extra Money too.
*[[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Asilan Pasalan/Assassilan Pasalan]] - Can be used in tandem with Cyberpunk Cat for extremely reliable crowd-control.

